File name: e4-allow.png. Landscape, exactly 1536 x 1024. References: refs/desktop-details.jpg for rows and style.
Screen: the extension's welcome page, step 4 of 5, "Allow what your picks need". Centred column.
Mono label "OFF GRID AI · IN YOUR BROWSER". Title "Allow what your picks need". Muted line "Your browser asks once. Only for what you picked."
A glass list with two rows, each with a line icon, a name, a muted reason, and a small button on the right:
Row 1: "Fix and rewrite" — "Read the text box you type in, on any site" — button "Allow" (quiet outline)
Row 2: "Chat" — "Read the page you ask about, only when you ask" — shows a small emerald check and muted text "Allowed"
Under the list, muted text "Change this any time in Settings."
Footer: 5-segment progress, segment 4 active, mono step name "ALLOW". Right: text buttons "Back" and "Skip", then the emerald primary button "Continue".
